The reason to consider waiting is that Apple is reportedly <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/08/apple-three-year-plan-to-reinvent-iphone/">working on a special 20th-anniversary iPhone</a> for release in September 2027, and rumors suggest that the device will feature the biggest redesign since the iPhone X in 2017.<br/>
<br/>
According to <em>Bloomberg</em>, the 20th-anniversary iPhone will have "glass edges that curve seamlessly into the display on all four sides."<br/>
<br/>
<em>The Information</em> reported that one of Apple's early 20th-anniversary iPhone prototypes <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/16/iphone-of-dreams-is-two-years-away/">lacked bezels around the screen</a>. The device had only a "narrow metal band running around the midpoint of the device's edge, where the buttons sit."<br/>
<br/>
Apple has also aimed for the device to have no cutouts in the screen, according to <em>The Information</em>, but it is unclear if the company will be able to move both the front camera and the Face ID system under the screen by next year.<br/>
<br/>
